lse,"inbound_outcome_count":null,"continuous_range":null},"group_rank":null,"coherence_links":null,"coherence_link_aggregations":null,"description":"The [Nobel Peace Prize](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/) is an internationally recognised award to&#x20;\n\n> the person who shall have done the most or the best work for fraternity between nations, the abolition or reduction of standing armies and for the holding and promotion of peace congresses.\n\nA total of [287 candidates have been nominated](https://www.nobelprize.org/nomination/peace/) for this year’s Prize. Of those, 208 are individuals and 79 are organisations. However, [disclosure of information about nominations is restricted](https://www.nobelprize.org/nomination/peace/), which leads to much speculation about the [possible candidates](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Nobel_Peace_Prize).&#x20;\n\nSince its Inception in 1901, the Nobel Peace Prize has been [awarded 106 times to 143 laureates](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/lists/all-nobel-peace-prizes/), consisting of 112 individuals and 31 organisations. [Seventy-two peace prizes](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/facts/facts-on-the-nobel-peace-prize/) have been awarded to one laureate only, and 34 prizes have been shared by two or three laureates. The 2025 peace laureate was [Maria Corina Machado](https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2025/summary/).","resolution_criteria":"This question will resolve as the recipient of the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize, expected to be announced by the Norwegian Nobel Committee on October 9, 2026.\n\nIf the prize is awarded to an individual not named in the listed options, this question will resolve as **Other individual**. If it is awarded to a non-individual recipient not named in the listed options, it will resolve as **Other organization**.\n\nIf no prize is awarded for any reason this question will be **annulled**.","fine_print":"If the prize is shared, this question will resolve as the option naming one of th